# The entire ~/.claude dir is co-managed by the Claude Code runtime + agent
# environment (settings, enabledPlugins, hooks, plugin state, caches, transcripts
# are all rewritten at runtime). Tracking it caused recurring `chezmoi update`
# conflicts, so the whole directory is left unmanaged.
#
# Exception: ~/.claude/output-styles/*.md holds portable, machine-independent
# output styles that Claude Code loads at user scope. Nothing rewrites them at
# runtime, so they are safe to track. Re-including a child needs the parent glob
# (`.claude/*`) and an explicit un-ignore of each directory on the way down; a
# bare `.claude` ignore cannot be negated.
.claude/*
!.claude/output-styles
.claude/output-styles/*
!.claude/output-styles/*.md
